<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan accepts 4.95 bln rupees in bond operation.</title>
<headline>Pakistan accepts 4.95 bln rupees in bond operation.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it had accepted 4.95 billion rupees in a special open market operation in Short-Term Federal Bonds on Saturday. Following are the results:</p>
<p>			  Offered	 Accepted	Max cut-off</p>
<p> Outright sales     3.725	   3.55	    16.50 pct</p>
<p> Five-month	   1.4	     1.4	     16.45 pct</p>
<p> Three-month	  Nil	     Nil	     Nil</p>
<p> One-month	    Nil	     Nil	     Nil</p>
<p>Total (bln rupees) 5.125 4.95</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
